{{!--
    One Consequence track.

    A partial rather than two copies of the same markup, because a Thread draws
    this in two places that have nothing else in common: once under the whole row
    when the complication belongs to the situation, and once inside each contender
    when the GM asked for one per side. Those live in different loops and would
    otherwise drift the first time either was touched.

    IT MIRRORS THE READING IT STANDS UNDER. `isPips` is true only on a Clock
    Thread, where the reading above this one is counted in dots the table can see
    — a smooth bar beside them would be two kinds of number sharing a row. Every
    other mode gets the bar. The decision is made in logic/progress.mjs
    `consequenceIsPips` and arrives here already answered.

    `showValues` and the absence of `pips` are the hideValues rule, owned by
    projectClock: a withheld clock falls back to a plain bar, because four filled
    dots out of six IS the number and counting them is not a workaround.

    THE LABEL IS THE CONTROL. There is no button at the end of this row. The
    reading it stands under has nothing there — a Clock's pips and a pool's bar
    are read, not pressed — so a + parked in that column put this track's number
    one button-width away from the number above it, and the two stopped reading
    as a column. The word that names the pile is what gets pressed instead. It
    stays a real <button>, so it answers to the keyboard like every other control
    here, and it is drawn only when this reader may push at all.

    Parameters: `track` (the reading), `threadId`, `forceId` ("" for the shared
    one — it lands in data-force-id, which the push handler reads as null).
--}}
<div class="rsr-consequence{{#if track.isFull}} is-full{{/if}}">
    {{#if track.canPush}}
    <button type="button" class="rsr-consequence-label" data-action="pushThread"
            name="push-consequence-{{threadId}}-{{forceId}}"
            data-thread-id="{{threadId}}" data-force-id="{{forceId}}"
            data-track="consequence"
            data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.pushConsequenceHint'}}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" inert></i>
        {{localize "RSR.thread.consequence"}}
    </button>
    {{else}}
    <span class="rsr-consequence-label">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" inert></i>
        {{localize "RSR.thread.consequence"}}
    </span>
    {{/if}}

    {{#if track.isPips}}
        {{#if track.pips}}
        <span class="rsr-pips rsr-pips-consequence">
            {{#each track.pips}}<i class="rsr-pip{{#if this.filled}} is-filled{{/if}}"></i>{{/each}}
        </span>
        {{else}}
        <span class="rsr-bar">
            <span class="rsr-bar-fill" style="width: {{track.percent}}%"></span>
        </span>
        {{/if}}
    {{else}}
    <span class="rsr-bar">
        <span class="rsr-bar-fill" style="width: {{track.percent}}%"></span>
    </span>
    {{/if}}

    {{#if track.showValues}}
    <span class="rsr-bar-value">{{track.current}}<span class="rsr-of">/{{track.total}}</span></span>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- At its line. Said here rather than only in the row's foot because a
          Contested Thread can have several of these and only one of them full,
          and a badge at the bottom could not say which. --}}
    {{#if track.isFull}}
    <span class="rsr-ready rsr-ready-consequence">{{localize "RSR.thread.consequenceFull"}}</span>
    {{/if}}
</div>
